message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Passive Through-Wall Human Sensing with Commodity WiFi Channel State Information: A Digital-Twin Study"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sabilly"
    given-names: "Ikhlas"
    email: "ikhlas.sabilly@gmail.com"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
license-url: "LICENSE"
keywords:
  - WiFi sensing
  - channel state information
  - through-wall sensing
  - digital twin
  - ray tracing
  - Sionna RT
  - ESP32
  - CSI ratio
  - presence detection
  - respiration monitoring
  - indoor localisation
abstract: >-
  A digital-twin study of passive through-wall human sensing with commodity WiFi CSI: a Blender model of a
  one-bedroom flat with articulated occupants, Sionna RT ray tracing of every link, an ESP32-class receiver
  model with interference, and pre-registered detectors for motion, breathing, bed occupancy and room-level
  tracking, checked against public real ESP32 recordings.
